# a-tower-brought-back — plan 17 T1 + T2, the upkeep loop as the player
# meets it.
#
# Before plan 17 a tower was a one-shot resource: thirty shots and black
# for the rest of the run, which is why plan 16 W4 measured the authored
# seven-wave list playing FOUR and falling with every tower spent.
#
# This file plays both halves of the answer through the real seam:
#
#   1. the REBUILD — the player stands beside a black tower for 20 s and
#      it fires again; no key is pressed, because repair is a POSITION
#   2. the TRANSPLANT — a spare top carried from a second tower goes on
#      instantly, and the magazine travels WITH it
#
# ⚠ The spare tower at (-4, 0) is eighteen hexes from the spawn marker,
# so it is permanently outside a tower's range of 15 and never fires a
# shot.  That is what makes its top a spare rather than a loss — and
# `plans/17` § T3 measures what happens when it is NOT: ferrying a
# firing tower's top forward costs the base fifty ticks.

echo a tower brought back: rebuilt by standing there, then transplanted

do toggle_mode

do cycle_kind
click 0 0
marker 0 0 target

do cycle_kind
click 4 0
click -4 0
marker 4 0 tower
marker -4 0 tower

do cycle_kind
do cycle_kind
do rotate
do rotate
do rotate
click 14 0
marker 14 0 spawn 3

count markers 4 4
do toggle_mode

palette 5
drag -6 -1 18 -1
drag -6 0 18 0
drag -6 1 18 1
count painted 75 75

# Nobody is in the world yet, and both towers are loaded.
top 4 0 on
top -4 0 on
shots 4 0 0 0

# ── The tower spends itself ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ TWO waves of eight, because one costs only seventeen shots — a
# wave big enough to empty a magazine in one go is also big enough to
# reach the core and end the run before the second half of this file.
wave 8
tick 60
wave 8
tick 60
shots 4 0 30 30

# ── 1. The REBUILD: stand there and it comes back ───────────────
#
# ⚠ No key is pressed.  The player parks inside the tower's own
# footprint and twenty seconds later the magazine is full.
park 4 0
tick 31
shots 4 0 0 0
top 4 0 on

# ── 2. The TRANSPLANT: a spare top, carried ─────────────────────
#
# ⚠ The player has to LEAVE first, and that is the mechanic rather than
# a scripting detail: standing beside the tower is what rebuilds it, so
# a player who never moves never has a black tower to swap.
drive -4 0
tick 8
vehicle -4 0

wave 8
tick 60
wave 8
tick 60
shots 4 0 30 30

# ⚠⚠ **And the "spare" is not idle after all** — it is eighteen hexes
# from the spawn marker, but the robots WALK to the core, which is four
# hexes away, so it has been shooting them off the doorstep.  Fifteen
# shots gone.  That is `plans/17` § T3's finding at the game level: a
# tower close enough to donate cheaply is close enough to be firing.
shots -4 0 15 15

take player
top -4 0 off

# ⚠ **Forty ticks for eight hexes, and the delay is the game.**  The
# approach is full of the tower's own dead, a body is 0.5 m and a hover
# unit climbs 0.4 — so the player has to CLEAR its way back in, one
# corpse at a time, through the kill zone it is trying to reload.  That
# is `ENEMY_MOVEMENT.md` § Bodies are terrain charging for the swap.
drive 4 0
tick 40
vehicle 4 0
drop player

# ⚠ **Instant** — `numbers.json` § tower.repair_time_top_transplant is
# 0.0 — and the tower it came from is a bare mast now.
#
# ⚠⚠ **But it arrives with FIFTEEN shots already gone**, because the
# magazine belongs to the TOP and travels with it (plan 17 T2).  A
# transplant moves firepower; it does not create any.  A run that read
# 0 here would mean detach-and-remount was a free repair, and the whole
# upkeep loop could be bypassed with two keypresses.
shots 4 0 15 15
top 4 0 on
top -4 0 off

# ⚠ And the SPENT top is lying where the swap dropped it, still
# remembering its thirty shots.  Nothing was overwritten.
cargo 1 1

snap t2_a_tower_brought_back
